  "selected": {
    "action": "IMPLEMENT",
    "tool": "skill_manage",
    "reason": "Record the fly-mode protocol and candidate-set traps as a reusable class-level skill.",
    "args_preview": "{\"operations\":[{\"action\":\"create\",\"category\":\"software-development\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: flymes-native-control\\ndescription: Use when Flymes native control is active and every tool call must be proposed for the fly to select. Propose candidates, execute the exact selection once.\\nmetadata:\\n  hermes:\\n    editorial_name: Flymes Native Control\\n    editorial_description: Working under flymes fly-mode selection - candidate proposals, exact execution, and the traps that stall a demo.\\n---\\n\\n# Flymes Native Control\\n\\nFlymes fly-mode hands tool selection to a human fly. The task block states when it is active; then you do not choose tools freely - you offer options and execute the winner.\\n\\n## Loop\\n\\n1. Call flymes_choose with command=propose and 2-6 candidates BEFORE every tool call. preferred_index marks your recommendation.\\n2. The response names the selected tool plus exact args, an action label, and a decision_id. Execute that tool with those exact args, once. Do not substitute, add flags, batch, or delegate.\\n3. Report the real result (exit code, output). If it failed, say so - the fly's selection governs the demo, including its mistakes.\\n4. Propose again for the next step; there is no multi-step authorization.\\n\\nAfter pause/resume call flymes_choose with command=current to fetch the pending selection, then execute it once. Never re-run a selection already executed.\\n\\n## Candidate shape (the guard is strict)\\n\\nEach candidate needs action, tool, args (an object), and reason.\\n\\n- action must be one of SEARCH, INSPECT, IMPLEMENT, TEST, REVIEW, FINISH.\\n- tool must be a normal Hermes tool name with an argument shape it actually accepts.\\n- Action categories must be DISTINCT within one proposal. Two candidates sharing a category are refused with 'Use distinct valid actions with normal tools, object args, and reasons' - the message does not name the broken rule, so check duplicate labels first.\\n- args must be an object even for one-parameter tools.\\n\\nA refusal authorizes nothing; fix the duplicate category and re-propose, never resend the identical payload.\\n\\n## Keep a doomed repeat out of the candidate set\\n\\nThe fly can pick the same verification command several rounds running, including before the fix it verifies has landed. Honour the selection, but it fails identically each time and the terminal tool raises a repeated-failure loop warning. Do not answer by re-proposing the same alternatives.\\n\\nWhen the fix has not landed yet, offer no candidate that can only fail: drop the verify option from that round's proposal and keep only productive actions (the edit, a read, a search). Verification returns to the candidate set the round after the edit lands. This keeps every selectable option actionable without overriding the fly.\\n\\nKeep the sequence honest otherwise: reproduce the defect, minimal edit, verify, report. Stalling rounds are a selection artifact worth one short note to the user, not a reason to skip the fly.\\n\\n## Reporting\\n\\nShort and factual: path touched, one-line diff, before/after evidence, the command that proves it. Never claim a check passed without the run showing it.\\n\",\"name\":\"flymes-native-control\"}]}",
    "args_truncated": false
  },
